description.narrative:
This project amplifies the voices of intersex youth in Coast Kenya through community mobilization, capacity building, and policy advocacy. We will build a network of 50 intersex youth advocates through leadership training while providing peer support groups offering safe spaces for connection, mentorship, and psychosocial support.

Community education will reach over 200 stakeholders - parents, teachers, and healthcare workers through dialogues aimed at combating harmful practices.

Youth-led policy forums will engage government officials to advocate for intersex-inclusive legal protections. We will develop accessible multimedia advocacy materials centering intersex youth experiences and amplify intersex voices through local radio programs.

Throughout all activities, intersex youth will co-design strategies, lead implementation, and directly engage policymakers, transforming from isolated individuals experiencing marginalization into a empowered movement advocating for representation.

Goal: Empower intersex youth in Coast Kenya as confident advocates shaping inclusive policies and fostering community acceptance.

Objectives:

(1) Build capacity of 50 intersex youth advocates aged 15-35;

(2) Reduce stigma through education reaching 200+ stakeholders across Coast Region;

(3) Influence policy for intersex protections and recognition.



Activities:

Monthly advocacy training;
peer support groups with mentorship;
community dialogues in Kilifi and Mombasa;
youth-led policy forums with county officials;
multimedia advocacy toolkits;
national youth policy consultations.
